Volunteer Program at PE Insights

Nordic's Largest PE Conference. Stockholm, November 24th &amp; 25th 2027

&nbsp;

Ready to take a major leap towards private equity, M&amp;A, banking or consulting? This is your chance to get a view behind the scenes of the world’s largest private equity community and be part of the volunteer team shaping the future of finance.

Challenge yourself to go outside your comfort zone with likeminded individuals who for two days will be your partners in the trenches facilitating the room of top-of-the pyramid PE professionals.

&nbsp;

Why Private Equity Insights

Private Equity Insights is the world’s largest Private Equity community with 1m PE professionals, delivering impact through 12 global PE conferences with thousands of the most world’s best investors and operators such as Blackstone, BlackRock, Apollo, Carlyle, CVC, KKR, and many more.&nbsp;

Private Equity Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large-scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, finance, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 5 media companies and exited 1.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What we offer you

You’ll be supporting the Private Equity Insights team in delivering the conference for sharp insights and inspiration, and outstanding network opportunities for the PE professionals we serve. Among other things the opportunity offer:

• Peer network: you join a select group of ambitious volunteers who will keep crossing your path for the next 40 years working in the industry.

• Insider knowledge. Where the day allows, you can sit in on panels, the same ones attendees come to hear. In fact, we encourage you to do so.

• Confidence under pressure: after two demanding conference days, high-stakes moments at work will feel easier.

• Master persuasion: learn to influence high-caliber professionals to deliver win-win results.&nbsp;

• A certificate to show on your CV and LinkedIn that you volunteered at Private Equity Insights.&nbsp;

• Fuel: food and refreshments on both days.

• Global programme: The long term opportunity to lead teams and become the person who shows the way for others, or even join Private Equity Insights full time.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your responsibilities

This is hands-on, operational work focusing on making the conference run. The work changes hour by hour, and you are expected to step in and help wherever the conference needs you.

&nbsp;

What the future hold for you with PE Insights&nbsp;

Whether you are with us for 1 conference or 10+, we believe this lays the foundation for a very successful career.&nbsp;

Exceptional volunteers have in the past been offered roles at Private Equity Insights, such as Investor Relations or Entrepreneur in Residence.

Others have gone on to join firms such as McKinsey, BCG, JP Morgan, Deutsche Bank, Ardian and Verdane.

&nbsp;

What we expect from you

We are looking for final-year undergraduates, master's students and early-career professionals with an interest in private equity, M&amp;A, banking, consulting or conferences. We expect you to:

• Have a relentless drive to become the very best at what you do

• Bring outstanding energy and a positive mindset from the first hour to the last

• Set aside 2 full days for the conference + online training leading up to

• Be curious to learn from top private equity professionals

• Stand out as the person others want beside them on a hard day

• Speak English at a professional level. Spanish is a plus

&nbsp;

This is an unpaid role. Applicants from outside Stockholm are welcome. You fully arrange your own travel and accommodation.&nbsp;

We review every application and invite shortlisted candidates to a short call. If you hold yourself to the standard described here, apply.

About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A hybrid working model &nbsp;

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around three days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process. &nbsp;

“This is a Contract role - Duration approx. 3 months” &nbsp;

What does Screen Producer do at WPP Production? &nbsp;

The Screen Producer supports the Lead Screen Producer on the creation, production and delivery of screen imagery, while balancing production capacity and control of scope, ensuring the consistency and accuracy of UI across product imagery for the entire studio. You will maintain a close partnership with producer partners across multiple functions to ensure precise tracking of all screen creative needs. You will partner with the Lead Screen Producer on the production of screen images by working with Creative and Production teams to plan, inform, track, and drive deadlines for new and existing screens.&nbsp; &nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Support the day-to-day screen creative and production process, including briefing, tracking, quality assurance, course correction, and delivery &nbsp;

• Partner with your Lead Screen Producer to build a foundation of product specific UI knowledge &nbsp;

• Partner with the Screen Creative team, briefing and tracking with them on all screen creative needs for all functional teams &nbsp;

• Direct the Screen Content Program Manager on daily screen production priorities and needs &nbsp;

• Provide guidance for the imagery requested by functional teams specific to each project as well as on accuracy and/or approval routes &nbsp;

• Work within a flat hierarchy supporting Creatives, Producers, and Production teams to help them succeed together &nbsp;

• Be someone who is proactive and has a go getter attitude, who is looking for and open to new ways of working &nbsp;

Requirements &nbsp;

• Have five to eight years of production experience at a creative agency &nbsp;

• Bring extensive experience in marketing content execution, experience design, localization, and you understand how to be a strong partner to the creative teams &nbsp;

• Have expertise in building real, positive relationships with creatives and producers who span many fields, including advertising, video, interactive, print, and retail &nbsp;

• Are experienced with guiding and shaping the production process across a variety of media, including print, interactive, and video &nbsp;

• Have project management experience at an ad agency production facility or equivalent &nbsp;

• React quickly to new information, opinions, and direction, and strategically pivot when necessary &nbsp;

• Love people and enjoy collaborating with team members &nbsp;

• Bachelor’s degree required. Advanced degree and certifications in applicable fields a plus

